It's always good to reduce the possibility of NULL values as they need special attention when constructing queries
They are only appropriate when database need to store incomplete data
#To test null values in a column
##Query

Select column, another_column
from mytable
Where column is NULL/NOT NULL
And/or other condition
And/or ....;

Example 
Find the name  and role of all employees who have not been assigned to a building

Select name, role, building
from Employees
Where building is NULL;

Find the building name that hold no employees

Select Building_name
from Buildings
LEFT JOIN employees
on buildings.name= Building
where role is NULL;


